		{"id":"ed98c7957beff767","type":"text","text":"Takeaways:\n* vector fields as force fields using noise\n* Procedural modeling for initializing RBD simulation","x":4354,"y":-631,"width":396,"height":250},
		{"id":"0ab5c39c9bb9f1e8","type":"text","text":"Further learning","x":5261,"y":-630,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"0500325fa9ba2fc3","type":"link","url":"https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/mpm/index.html","x":-1070,"y":239,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"d0885525b36436d8","type":"link","url":"https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/vellum/index.html","x":-1070,"y":699,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"369f8f485ef7bfc7","type":"text","text":"Houdini RBD:\n* Built-in RBD\n* Bullet RBD\n* Open Dynamics Engine\n* MPM\n* Vellum (Position based dynamics)","x":-1040,"y":-1046,"width":340,"height":240},
		{"id":"2c3bca4218e26a1a","type":"link","url":"https://extensions.blender.org/add-ons/cell-fracture/","x":530,"y":-141,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"f5d2c0b7f5751694","type":"text","text":"Where it is used","x":-3254,"y":-614,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"5c85161e8c3acfdf","type":"text","text":"When to use it","x":-2676,"y":-614,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"24398086df771a3d","type":"text","text":"General concepts","x":-1922,"y":-756,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"1e4ba5e67bb31c7d","type":"text","text":"The [Rigid Body solver](https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/dop/rigidbodysolver.html \"Sets and configures a Rigid Body Dynamics solver.\") simulates the motion and collisions of objects as if they were hard, solid objects (as opposed to other types of simulated objects such as fluids, cloth, and soft bodies)","x":-2038,"y":-614,"width":482,"height":136},
		{"id":"c104b6bd7d69b973","type":"link","url":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1145/2556700.2556713?casa_token=9i_sM2Dud3wAAAAA%3AN5XFUTjcGkPoqWebxFAOwVgOPiLx8l8qJ6QcPNzaGgYC-nmH-8mtR9Z2qF9yTnMn4Tu68DTGvTc","x":-1997,"y":-381,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"0169d678c039d258","type":"text","text":"This is the first lecture introducing physical simulation which will be the topic for next 4 lectures: \n* Solids\n\t* Rigid body\n\t* Deformable body\n* Fluids:\n\t* Liquid\n\t* Gas\n\nThe procedural modeling and phyiscal simulation:\n* Procedurally define parameters and initial state of simulation\n* Use results of physicals simulation for procedural modeling","x":-4430,"y":-716,"width":820,"height":397,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"2108efbeff1ff53a","type":"link","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xdC7k_LslgA","x":-2950,"y":-387,"width":640,"height":360},
		{"id":"438fc60862dba113","type":"link","url":"https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/vellum/index.html","x":-981,"y":1941,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"f22a2569c8ba2f41","type":"link","url":"https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/finiteelements/index.html","x":-981,"y":2401,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"c4aa7d96ef4d5650","type":"link","url":"https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/mpm/index.html","x":-981,"y":2861,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"5bd4881fe5f5cd38","type":"link","url":"https://docs.blender.org/manual/en/latest/physics/soft_body/index.html","x":853,"y":1801,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"f838d25137deed1d","type":"text","text":"Blender Deformable body","x":928,"y":1587,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"30190e0e0840585a","type":"text","text":"Blender deformable body examples\n* Inflating with collisions: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IofA3OA3eIk - quite unstable\n* Cloth: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tMRi32Las1U - works great\n* ","x":1740,"y":1569,"width":836,"height":332},
		{"id":"b15360bc302205a4","type":"text","text":"Vellum simulation is build using one solver and number of constraints which defined behavior:\n* Ballon\n* Cloth\n* Hair\n* Fluid\n* Grain\n* Softbody\n* Collisions\n* Pinning\n\nGreat explanation: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=h0iAAY8Zpq0","x":2922,"y":2197,"width":624,"height":384},
